title: Edit several at once
intro: With several entities selected, the Inspector edits them all together: the components they share, with values that differ shown as mixed.
project: Empty | Multi Edit

# Three gems in different colors and places; the green one also glows.
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Red Gem
set: Sprite.Tint = #FF004D
set: Transform.Position = -3, 0, 0
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Blue Gem
set: Sprite.Tint = #29ADFF
set: Transform.Position = 0, 1, 0
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Green Gem
set: Sprite.Tint = #00E436
set: Transform.Position = 3, -1, 0
add: Light
look: 0, 0, 5

chapter: What they share | Select several, see them together
say: Here are three gems, each its own color, in its own place.
select: Red Gem
select: Ctrl+Blue Gem
select: Ctrl+Green Gem
expectselected: Red Gem, Blue Gem, Green Gem
explain: panel:Inspector | Three entities | With all three selected, the Inspector shows them together. It edits the components all three have; only the green gem has a light, so that one is greyed, on 1 of 3.
expectpartial: Light = on 1 of 3
expectmixed: Sprite.Tint
explain: field:Sprite.Tint | Mixed | Their colors differ, so the tint shows a dash rather than picking one of them.

chapter: Change them all | One value, every entity, one undo step
set: Sprite.Tint = #FFEC27
expectvalue: Red Gem.Sprite.Tint = #FFEC27
expectvalue: Blue Gem.Sprite.Tint = #FFEC27
expectvalue: Green Gem.Sprite.Tint = #FFEC27
explain: scene | All gold | Type one color, and every gem takes it.
say: It's a single step to undo, and each gem gets its own color back.
key: Ctrl+Z
expectvalue: Red Gem.Sprite.Tint = #FF004D
expectvalue: Green Gem.Sprite.Tint = #00E436
expectmixed: Sprite.Tint
expectat: Red Gem = -3, 0
expectat: Blue Gem = 0, 1
expectat: Green Gem = 3, -1
expectmixed: Transform.Position.Y
set: Transform.Position.Y = 2
expectat: Red Gem = -3, 2
expectat: Blue Gem = 0, 2
expectat: Green Gem = 3, 2
explain: world:-4.5, 3.5, 4.5, 0.5 | Lined up | Each axis of a position is its own field. Setting Y lines the gems up in a row, and each keeps its own X.

chapter: Adding to all of them | Add Component works on every one
add: Health
set: Health.Max = 5
expectvalue: Red Gem.Health.Max = 5
expectvalue: Blue Gem.Health.Max = 5
expectvalue: Green Gem.Health.Max = 5
explain: component:Health | Health on all three | Add Component puts a Health on every gem, and setting its Max sets them all.
say: Editing a row of enemies, a set of platforms or a whole level's coins is now one change instead of one per entity.
